Z||000005||EdsB52||08-26-2001||01:21 AM||||I think it's objective to say we lost Viet Nam. Hate to say it, but when you start a fight and walk away, I think that's recorded as a loss. We could have "won," but we would have had to go nuclear; Charlie was just too sneaky in their own back yard. Kudos to all brave soldiers; middle fingers to all greasy politicians that thought it was a good idea to trade 52,000 people for military manufacturers' profits.||||reg||1
